{
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "description": "Where content-service sends each document for text extraction, and why.\n\nExtraction is routed by file extension: SPREADSHEET_EXTENSIONS goes to xlsxparser over gRPC, TIKA_EXTENSIONS to a dedicated Tika 4.x instance (processing-systems tikaContent), and everything else to xberg. The lists may overlap \u2014 an extension goes to the first backend that both claims it and could be built \u2014 so a document silently changing backend is a normal failure mode, and the fallback row is how you see it.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "liveNow": false,
  "panels": [
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 100,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Where documents are processed",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Which backend actually parsed each document, per second.\n\n- kreuzberg \u2014 xberg, the default extractor: everything no route claims.\n- tika_routed \u2014 Tika as a routed extractor (TIKA_EXTENSIONS), the foreground parse.\n- spreadsheet \u2014 xlsxparser over gRPC (SPREADSHEET_EXTENSIONS).\n- tika \u2014 the SAMPLED COMPARISON second parse only, not a routing destination. It appears here so it is not mistaken for routed traffic; it is zero unless EXTRACTION_COMPARISON_ENABLED is on.\n\nA routed series at zero while its extensions are being requested is the thing to chase \u2014 see the fallback row below for why.",
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Extractions by parser_kind",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "fillOpacity": 20,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (parser_kind) (rate(content_extraction_total{namespace=\"$namespace\", job=\"$job\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{parser_kind}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "The same data as a proportion, so a routing change is visible as a shift rather than as a change in absolute volume. Sums to 1 while comparison is off; above 1 when it is on, because a sampled document is parsed twice.",
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Share of documents by parser_kind",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "fillOpacity": 20,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "unit": "percentunit"
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (parser_kind) (rate(content_extraction_total{namespace=\"$namespace\", job=\"$job\"}[5m]))\n  / scalar(sum(rate(content_extraction_total{namespace=\"$namespace\", job=\"$job\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{parser_kind}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Extension \u2192 parser_kind (selected range)",
      "description": "Which backend served each file type over the dashboard range. This is the panel that answers 'are spreadsheets actually going where I configured them'. An extension appearing under kreuzberg that you expected under spreadsheet or tika_routed means it fell back \u2014 the reason is in the row below.\n\nextension is bounded by EXTRACTION_COMPARISON_EXTENSION_WHITELIST; anything off that list shows as 'other', and a file with no extension as 'unknown'.",
      "type": "table",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "cellOptions": {
              "type": "auto"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true,
        "sortBy": [
          {
            "desc": true,
            "displayName": "Value"
          }
        ]
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "sum by (extension, parser_kind) (increase(content_extraction_total{namespace=\"$namespace\", job=\"$job\"}[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "id": 200,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Routed fallbacks \u2014 why a routed extractor did not run",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Requests that were MEANT for a routed extractor and took the default one instead.\n\n- not_registered \u2014 the extractor could not be built at startup: no address, no client in this image, or an unreachable backend. A FAULT. Sustained non-zero means a backend is down and its documents are quietly being parsed by xberg.\n- not_applicable \u2014 the extractor is routed for that extension but cannot serve that request, today meaning an output format it does not produce (xlsxparser is markdown-only, Tika has no djot). Expected traffic, not a fault \u2014 this is what explains a quiet routed extractor when callers are asking for a format it cannot make.\n\nThe document is still extracted either way; only the backend differs.",
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Fallbacks by extractor and reason",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (extractor, reason) (rate(content_extraction_routed_fallback_total{namespace=\"$namespace\", job=\"$job\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{extractor}} \u2014 {{reason}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Should be ZERO. Non-zero means a routed extractor is configured but was not built at startup, so its file types are silently taking the default extractor. Check the content-service startup log for 'routed extractor unavailable', and whether the backend Service exists and is reachable.",
      "id": 5,
      "title": "not_registered fallbacks",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 19
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "decimals": 2,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.0001
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum (rate(content_extraction_routed_fallback_total{namespace=\"$namespace\", job=\"$job\", reason=\"not_registered\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "not_registered",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Expected, not a fault. A steady rate here with a routed extractor at zero throughput means callers are asking for an output format that extractor cannot produce, so the default extractor is serving them correctly.",
      "id": 6,
      "title": "not_applicable fallbacks",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 19
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "decimals": 2,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum (rate(content_extraction_routed_fallback_total{namespace=\"$namespace\", job=\"$job\", reason=\"not_applicable\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "not_applicable",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Fraction of extractions served by a routed backend rather than the default one. Drops to zero when routing is off, or when every routed extractor fell back.",
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Routed share of extractions",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 23
