        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Non-success extractions per second, split by backend and classified status.\n\nStatus values come from the caller-facing taxonomy in docs/error-codes.md \u2014 corrupted, timeout, service_unavailable, file_too_large, unsupported_type, empty_content, canceled.\n\nfile_too_large on tika_routed specifically may mean the Tika write limit (tikaContent output-limits.writeLimit) truncated a document and content-service refused the partial result rather than caching it.",
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Failure rate by parser_kind",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
